# molecfit/esorex transient log
esorex.log

# RYA-396 NLTE-grid scrape checkpoints (intermediate)
data/nlte_grids/raw/

# RYA-402: Amarsi/GALAH PySME departure grids (multi-GB binaries; re-fetchable from the provenance JSON, never committed)
data/nlte_grids/**/*.grd
# RYA-410: the Zenodo download archives are transient (extracted then deleted) — never commit
data/nlte_grids/**/*.tar.gz
# RYA-426: UV conditioning manifests (per-star working artifacts, regenerable)
data/conditioning/

# Local, per-run intake debug traces (RYA-318) -- never committed.
debug/intake/

# RYA-774: regenerable band-measurement OUTPUTS. The generators are now on main
# (scripts/measure_band_profilefit.py, scripts/derive_band_products.py), so these are
# reproducible from the atlas and do not belong in git — the same move as debug/intake/
# (RYA-765) and the near-UV line list (RYA-759). This exists to stop a broad `git add`
# sweeping a local run's artifacts onto an unrelated branch, which is what stranded
# RYA-716 and contaminated RYA-759.
#
# NOT a policy that band products may never be committed: an intended DELIVERABLE is
# still `git add -f`-able and must then be registered in data/results/GENERATORS.yaml
# against its generator (RYA-686). Ignoring only changes the default from
# accidentally-tracked to deliberately-tracked.
data/measured/band_ew/
data/results/band_products/
data/results/fe_ir/
# RYA-759: generated near-UV synthesis line list (12 MB, regenerable in ~10s)
data/linelists/ispec_nearuv_*/atomic_lines.tsv

# RYA-789 — Elgueta 2026 (J/A+A/710/A111) reduced CRIRES+ spectra: 18 files, ~33 MB of
# bulk observational data. Sirius-only (RYA-567), md5-pinned in the committed MD5SUMS.txt
# (RYA-540) and re-fetchable with scripts/fetch_elgueta2026_vizier.py. The ReadMe, the
# three atomic line lists and the paper tables ARE committed (~1.6 MB) — they are the
# reference RYA-787 maps Fe lines from, and data/reference/ is a committed surface.
data/reference/elgueta2026_vizier/sp/
